A||N||8||Slapnutz2000||Nose badge removal/replacement||||1||
Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||10-13-2000||02:00 AM||||I have an 86 2m4 and I just bought a new nose badge. My question is - How do I remove the old badge without scratching/drilling anything?<BR>I have the correct adhesive to glue the new badge in place but I don't want to hurt the body while taking it out.<P>TIA!||||reg||1
Z||000001||sdm1964||10-13-2000||06:54 AM||||If i remember correctly, there is a dimple sticking out the back side with a push nut on it. You have to get to the underside of it and remove the push nut to get the badge off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbotom||10-13-2000||07:16 AM||||Thats correct, I just replaced mine last week after somebody swiped it. Broke it right off, the bastards! Anyway, it can be reached using a 10mmm socket without dissaembling anything else. Don't use the glue. It wasn't originally mounted with any.<BR>Also, I've discovered that SE and GT badges don't have the second dimple on the same side so they're not interchangable unless you break it off. The second dimple goes into the second hole of the fascia. It prevents the badge from rotating in place. A new badge goes for about 20 bucks at the dealer.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-13-2000||08:31 AM||||HEH  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> love your e-mail address Turbotom!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> you have a turbotom set up on a Z?<P> My 86 SE nose had that dimple in it? i glas'd over it and filled in the other hole (no badge) but mine had a press washer on the back? you might want to check and be sure you have a nut on the badge cause if you have the LAME press washer you Have to take the nose off to cut the washer... ( i did anyways)||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-13-2000||08:53 AM||||So far the ones I've seen have a stamped tin nut on the back. More of a self threading nut than a push nut. Off top of my head I thougt they where 13mm but it's no big deal either way. you don't need the whole nose off to get at them. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbotom||10-13-2000||11:28 AM||||Thanks 1FST2M6, yes I am new to this board. I'm the sucker who won the bid on that stage 2 turbo kit on ebay (see posts in "The Mall"). Hence the name turbotom, although my mane is Mike not Tom. Make sense so far? hehe. Theogre is right, it is a "self - threading stamped tin nut". Both my cars are '87's and have this nut holding down the emblem to the nose. Perhaps ealier cars use a press washer, whatever. Anyway glad to be on board. Best board out there for Fiero owners. Pennock RULES!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||2xsess||10-15-2000||12:01 AM||||Why did you call yourself a sucker turbotom?<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||turbotom||10-15-2000||01:35 AM||||I call myself a "sucker" simply for the fact that I'm a sucker for fine things such as an expensive option for the Fiero V6 engine. Very expensive. How many people do you know who shelled out the bucks for this kit?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Philphine||10-15-2000||05:18 PM||||yep. self threading nut on '84s too. just did it a few hours ago. i had the whole nose off though.||||reg||1
